strated by carrying out the system  suitability test to ensure that the toc  analyzer can successfully analyze  the full range of organic materials  expected to be present in pharmaceutical  grade waters  the ability to successfully measure the  presence of inside measured toc in the  presence of large amounts of potentially  interfering inorganic carbon or tic  it's demonstrated by challenging the  alloys with two samples  one they both contain the same amount of  organic carbon but one of them contains  large amounts of inorganic carbon in the  form of dissolved co2 which is typically  how he's finding pure dried water  so if the analyzer can report the same  toc results from both samples that is  deemed to have passed successfully  the qbd 1200 can handle very high levels  of tic because it completely sparges it  or push it out from the sample before  attempting to measure toc  once the tic is sparged from the sample  the uv lamp is turned on and the  analysis of toc  commences  the qbd therefore take makes the direct  measurement of toc not a calculated one  so it actually measures toc directly not  calculating it and so the plus or minus  two percent tolerance on the sensor that  the qbd uses  means for example as there might be  potentially a plus or minus two parts  per billion potential error  in a sample containing 100 ppb of toc  and this is despite the presence of  relatively large amounts of gic  now the limit of detection is the  smallest amount of a substance the  analyzer can detect  but not necessarily accurately report  whereas the limit of quantitation is the  smallest amount of a substance that  analyzer will not only detect with our  accurate accurately measure and report  and neither of these of course is very  easy to do in the real world especially  with um a limited detection of 0.4 ppb  so what ith q2 does it provides guidance  on how to calculate the limited  detection and limited quantitation based  on the standard deviation of the results